// vcsc-cc1 -I .
// expectfail
// expecterr: array size must be greater than zero, not 0
//
// A zero-length array used to be accepted silently and produced a zero-sized
// object. That made `extern const uint8_t guard[0]` look like a compile-time
// guard while doing nothing at all: the declaration was never diagnosed, the
// symbol was never allocated, and code guarded by it built and ran with the
// guard permanently inactive.  Several compile-time guards in the tree were
// written that way.
include "machine_6502.c26"
extern const uint8_t zero_length_declaration[0];
void main(void) { }